        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 12398 (signed 1982-12-31; 48 FR 377) was read in full in the held Federal Register text jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_12398.txt. It amends Executive Order 12369 (President’s Private Sector Survey on Cost Control): the lead recital and instruction, subsection (a) (membership of not more than 170) and subsection (b) (Committee terminates on 1983-06-30 unless sooner extended). The dossier evidence ACT:EO:12398>EO:12553 (agent-located, independently reviewed) was re-read against the held EO 12553 text, whose revocation table lists 12398. Later orders read in their held Federal Register texts: EO 12429 (signed 1983-06-28) restates section 4(b) with the date 1983-10-30; EO 12447 (signed 1983-10-27) with 1983-12-31; EO 12455 (signed 1983-12-29) with 1984-01-31, each unless sooner extended. EO 12534 (1985-09-30) revokes the parent EO 12369 without naming EO 12398. Machine searches read: U.S. Code 0 hits, eCFR 0 hits, Federal Register catalog hits not decisive. Under the owner rulings of 2026-10-21 (unnamed instruments and strike-and-insert) and 2026-10-28 the end is EO 12553, the amendments of section 4(b) are later events recorded in the reasons, and the parent revocation and the last held scheduled sunset are disclosed candidates.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Candidates tested for an earlier end: (1) the section 4(b) sunset restated here (1983-06-30, unless sooner extended) was extended by EO 12429, EO 12447 and EO 12455, so it is not the end; the last held scheduled sunset is 1984-01-31 (EO 12455, unless sooner extended) and no held source shows whether it was extended again or when the Committee in fact ceased. (2) EO 12534 revokes the parent EO 12369 effective 1985-09-30 but names neither EO 12398 nor the other amending orders; disclosed under the owner ruling on unnamed instruments. (3) Only EO 12553 names EO 12398 among the held later orders.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"Subsection (a) (membership limit) and subsection (b) (termination date) are independent amendments of different sections of EO 12369, but both depend on the Committee and end together when the order is revoked. The lead clause is the amending instruction.\",\"savings_check\":\"Read for savings: EO 12553 has no savings clause in its enacting sentence. Appointments of members and Committee work are accrued effects; no standing command remains.\",\"scope_check\":\"Three clauses: the lead instruction to amend EO 12369, subsection (a) on membership, and subsection (b) on the termination sentence. EO 12429, EO 12447 and EO 12455 restate only section 4(b); nothing held amends the lead or subsection (a). EO 12553 revokes the whole order.\"}",
